# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAFETY: this directory is the working tree of the PUBLIC repo
#   github.com/TokkatheDj/party-command-games
# Most of what lives in this folder is PRIVATE work that merely shares the
# directory. This file is an ALLOW-LIST: everything at the top level is
# ignored unless it is named below. A new project folder appearing here is
# therefore ignored by default -- `git add -A` cannot publish it by accident.
#
# History: a deny-list missed new projects twice (2026-07-29, 2026-08-07) and
# a third time by 2026-08-16 (consulting/, finance-doc-system/, roadside-job-
# log/, ti-calcs/, *.design/, skills/ were all sitting untracked and
# publishable). Flipped to this allow-list on 2026-08-16. Verified at the
# time that the allowed entries below were exactly the set already tracked
# (`git ls-files | cut -d/ -f1 | sort -u`), so nothing changed in history.
#
# To PUBLISH a new folder deliberately: add a `!/name/` line below, then
# `git add name`. Nothing else is needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Ignore everything at the top level...
/*

# ...except the party-games site itself:
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/index.html
!/party.html
!/scoreboard-mobile.png
!/build-my-app/
!/cowork apps/

# Rules that still apply INSIDE the allowed folders
# (.claude/ = local Claude Code state, worktrees, session screenshots;
#  the few skill files already tracked there stay tracked - ignore rules
#  never affect files git already knows about)
# (cowork apps/ also has its own .gitignore for its content folders)
.netlify
.claude/
*.log
.godot/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
